            <ArticleTitle>Essential thrombocythemia and coronary artery disease.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>933-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>An unusual case of essential thrombocythemia in a young man presenting with progressive angina pectoris is presented. Angiography revealed proximal left anterior descending artery stenosis. Successful percutaneous transluminal angioplasty along with antiplatelet therapy and a calcium channel blocking drug have rendered this patient asymptomatic.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
